          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Pick your epoxy floor color based on <strong class="text-white">how you actually use the garage</strong>, not just how a sample chip looks under showroom lighting. Gray and tan are the low-maintenance, resale-safe defaults for a reason — they hide the widest range of everyday mess. Darker colors and bold hues look fantastic in a garage that gets swept regularly and isn't baking in direct sun, but they demand more upkeep and a stronger personal commitment to the look. There's no wrong color, only a color that matches — or doesn't match — how your garage actually gets lived in.
